    "summary": "This Knoevenagel condensation reaction was successfully translated from batch to continuous flow processing using a glass chromatography column reactor. The reaction proceeded via nucleophilic addition followed by dehydration at room temperature (25°C) with a residence time of 9 minutes and flow rate of 1.5 mL/min at 0.25 M concentration. The flow process achieved a 99% yield compared to 95.2% in the batch baseline, representing a 3.8 percentage point improvement. The enhanced performance in flow was achieved while significantly reducing reaction time from 10 minutes in batch to just 9 minutes residence time, demonstrating both improved efficiency and yield in the continuous process.",
